        <mxCell id="legend-control-text" value="pointer to an existing rule or integration ID" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontColor=#57606a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="344" y="870" width="280" height="20" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dataflow-note" value="Question: where does personal data go, and which flows cross a trust boundary? Crossings: flow-1 and flow-10 (staff devices into the service), flow-3 and flow-5 (the service and hospital core systems), and flow-8 and flow-9 (a third-party gateway). Each crossing is left for assess-threats.&lt;br&gt;Source: build-spec.md Domain model, Integrations and data (I1 to I3), Business rules BR1 and BR4, and messages M2 to M5.&lt;br&gt;Proposed. It is not a threat assessment, a penetration test, or a privacy assessment." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="910" width="1160" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
